# GOAD's sources are consumed on Linux even when you drive it from Windows:
# the azure/aws providers copy this tree to the ubuntu jumpbox, which runs the
# setup scripts and ansible from it.
#
# Cloned on Windows with core.autocrlf=true (the Git for Windows default),
# every file lands with CRLF. The jumpbox is then handed CRLF shell scripts:
#
#     ssh jumpbox "bash -s" < scripts/setup_azure.sh
#
# and bash treats the trailing \r as part of each command, so the whole script
# fails line by line:
#
#     bash: line 2: $'\r': command not found
#     E: Invalid operation update
#     /usr/bin/python3: No module named pip
#
# Nothing aborts, so provisioning continues to the point where ansible-playbook
# is missing and the lab looks like an ansible problem rather than a checkout
# problem.
#
# Force LF in the working tree regardless of platform. Binary files are still
# detected and left alone by text=auto.
* text=auto eol=lf
